        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: तरुः",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "तरुः (taruḥ) — \"a tree\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "You have had वनम्, a forest, for a long while now. तरुः (taruḥ) is one tree standing in it."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Sanskrit keeps several names for a tree — vṛkṣa, druma, and this one — and तरुः (taruḥ) is the shortest and the easiest to say. It ends in -uḥ, like गुरुः and वायुः, so you already know how it behaves."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One tree, picked out of a forest you already know."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
