        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: तृणम्",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "तृणम् (tṛṇam) — \"grass, a blade of grass\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "तृणम् (tṛṇam) covers a single blade and a whole field of it. It is the low green stuff a तरुः (taruḥ) stands in."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "English thorn is the same word: Old English thorn, Gothic thaurnus, from a shape like trnus, \"a stiff thing that grows up out of the ground\". Sanskrit kept the mild end of that meaning and Germanic kept the sharp end, which is a common way for one word to become two things."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A third growing thing, and the reason grass and a thorn are the same word."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
