          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: लता",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "लता (latā) — \"a creeper, a climbing plant\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "लता (latā) is anything that climbs rather than stands: a vine, a creeper, a trailing branch."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Sanskrit poetry pairs it with तरुः (taruḥ) so often that the two almost arrive together — the creeper and the tree it climbs. Unlike most of this chapter it has no European cousin worth naming; it is homegrown, and it went on to become one of the commonest given names in India. Ends in -आ, like तारा."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A fourth growing thing, and a name half of India answers to."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
