        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: दारु",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "दारु (dāru) — \"wood, timber\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "दारु (dāru) is the substance a तरुः (taruḥ) is made of."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It is one of the securest cousins in this book. English tree is it, and so are Gothic triu, Greek drus \"oak\", Welsh derwen and Russian derevo; through a Celtic word for one who knows the oak comes druid. English true and trust belong to the same family, on the old idea that to be true is to be as firm as a tree. Ends in short -u, like साधु."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Five growing things, and the tree standing inside the English word true."
            }
          ]
        },
